  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize pairs and consecutive suits when choosing your three cards. A low pair is often better than three high unconnected cards.\n\nThe 'Hidden' Kicker: If you have a choice of two identical pairs (e.g., two 8s and a 10 vs two 8s and a 4), always keep the highest kicker to win tie-breaking showdowns.\n\nDiscard Influence: Track which ranks are being mucked. If you see several players mucking 3s, the probability of someone holding a Prial of 3s (the top hand) drops significantly.",
    Player: "Prioritize pairs and consecutive suits when choosing your three cards. A low pair is often better than three high unconnected cards.\n\nThe 'Hidden' Kicker: If you have a choice of two identical pairs (e.g., two 8s and a 10 vs two 8s and a 4), always keep the highest kicker to win tie-breaking showdowns.\n\nDiscard Influence: Track which ranks are being mucked. If you see several players mucking 3s, the probability of someone holding a Prial of 3s (the top hand) drops significantly.",
